  "implementation": [
    "Prepare validates actor/base authority, supported graph/process/clock inputs, CRT transition, identity frontier and immutable retained request/resource/NI bindings before any authority write.",
    "An optional prepared melee frame transfers to the same transaction. Its service, actor and next clock must match. Clock advancement with an existing melee owner requires that companion. Owned body strike/reaction action conflicts and actor-clock rewinds reject.",
    "Commit revalidates current owner identity, actor values/life, graph, selected resource, melee state, clock and RNG, then publishes staged map nodes/swaps and process fields together. No contact allocation/consumption, resource loading, key traversal or renderer callbacks occur here.",
    "Cleared graphs retain their issued-identity frontier. Low-process cleanup accepts no new active-process authority. No save-format migration.",
    "retainSourceArtifact clones the exact parsed KF holder without a native info lease or backend lookup; an NI source may survive final info release and coexist with a new info loaded from replacement bytes."
  ],
